(SAMPLING METHODOLOGY FOR OFFICIAL SURVEYS) Tj T*
(National Statistical Office - training note) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. THE SAMPLING FRAME) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The sampling frame is the list of units from which a sample is actually drawn.) Tj T*
(Any mismatch between the frame and the target population produces coverage error,) Tj T*
(and coverage error cannot be repaired by weighting after the fact. Frames for) Tj T*
(household surveys in India are commonly built from Census enumeration blocks in) Tj T*
(urban areas and from village lists in rural areas.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. STRATIFICATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stratified random sampling divides the population into homogeneous strata and) Tj T*
(draws an independent sample within each stratum. When the strata are internally) Tj T*
(homogeneous with respect to the study variable, stratification reduces the) Tj T*
(variance of the estimator relative to simple random sampling of the same size.) Tj T*
(Allocation across strata may be proportional to stratum size, or optimal, in) Tj T*
(which case it also accounts for within-stratum variance and cost of enumeration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. PROBABILITY PROPORTIONAL TO SIZE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Probability proportional to size selection gives larger units a greater chance of) Tj T*
(inclusion. This improves efficiency when the study variable is correlated with) Tj T*
(the measure of size used for selection. In multi-stage designs, first-stage units) Tj T*
(such as villages or urban blocks are frequently selected with probability) Tj T*
(proportional to population, with a fixed number of households selected at the) Tj T*
(second stage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. WEIGHTING AND ESTIMATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The design weight of a unit is the reciprocal of its probability of selection.) Tj T*
(Design weights are adjusted for non-response and are often calibrated to known) Tj T*
(population totals so that survey estimates agree with external benchmarks such) Tj T*
(as projected population. Variance estimation must reflect the design: treating a) Tj T*
(multi-stage stratified sample as if it were simple random sampling understates) Tj T*
(standard errors, sometimes severely.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. NON-SAMPLING ERROR) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Non-sampling error includes measurement error, processing error and non-response.) Tj T*
(In large official surveys non-sampling error frequently exceeds sampling error in) Tj T*
(magnitude, and unlike sampling error it does not shrink as the sample grows. It) Tj T*
(is controlled through interviewer training, instrument design, supervision and) Tj T*
(independent re-interview of a subsample.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
