(6. DATA QUALITY, EDITING AND IMPUTATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Editing rules detect records that violate logical or arithmetic constraints.) Tj T*
(Selective editing concentrates limited review effort on the records whose) Tj T*
(correction would most change the published aggregate. Imputation replaces a) Tj T*
(missing value with a plausible substitute derived from responding units. The) Tj T*
(imputation method must be recorded, because imputed values add uncertainty that) Tj T*
(naive variance estimates ignore. Donor-based hot-deck imputation preserves the) Tj T*
(distribution of the variable better than mean imputation, which artificially) Tj T*
(reduces variance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. QUESTIONNAIRE AND FIELD OPERATIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A well designed questionnaire places sensitive questions late in the interview,) Tj T*
(after the respondent has committed time to the exercise and rapport has been) Tj T*
(established. Computer assisted personal interviewing enforces skip patterns and) Tj T*
(range checks at the point of collection, which removes an entire class of) Tj T*
(downstream editing work and shortens the interval between collection and release.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
